  I tried this recently, after filling the entire shop with pits for good 
measure, and got the message "The shopkeeper leaps and grabs your pack!"
so it isn't foolproof (though I'd imagine it's rare).

>What's your 'Easiest/best way to rob a job' ?

My favorite thieving item is the ring of conflict.  Not only does it
tend to reveal the swarms of mimics and keep the Keystone Kops busy
fighting each other, you can also use it to get out with a little
planning.  Keep the ring off when you're in the shop; sooner or later
some beast is going to follow you in (eyes, blobs, and other beasties
you can ignore are best).  Put the ring on and maneuver yourself and
the beastie so that the shopkeeper, getting out of your line-of-fire,
will move next to it, and run out of the shop while he's busy
fighting.  Problems:  this gets the shopkeeper mad at you more often than
not, and tends to get your pet killed.

Speaking of pets:  is there any way to keep your pet from attacking 
tamed jackals and the like?  It seems to rather defeat the point.  
